From 7017a16b99c64b946f443aa20fe8786d2c6815ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:56:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-25: Group Into a new panel / Ungroup -- Blend's
 Ctrl+G / Ctrl+Shift+G (0.25.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- 放進新 Panel (Ctrl+G, right-click): the selected components -- all in one
  parent -- get a new TPanel around them (Panel3 ..., no border, no
  background, a caption span like the generated ones), exactly their bounding
  box; they now count from it, so on the screen nothing moves. The probe
  measures the drawn sizes (a label without a width is as wide as its text).
  The panel takes the first one's place in the source.
- 解除群組 (Ctrl+Shift+G): the selected TPanel / TGroupBox's children (from
  its <div class="cli"> when it has one; its caption span / legend stay out)
  move into its parent, their left/top plus the container's place and border
  (the probe's clientLeft/Top), and the container goes.
- One WorkspaceEdit each; a locked one is refused; the new panel / the first
  child is selected.
- classOf(): the DFM's class, else the component tree's, else the source's
  generated title="name : TClass" -- so a panel made a moment ago (in no DFM,
  the tree not re-drawn yet) is known as a TPanel; used by ungroup, the
  toolbox, paste and the tree's drag and drop.
- lookAll now reports cl / ct (the box's border); htmlblock.firstPx.

Tests: lib 117, smoke 90 (spbSave + sbtExit into Panel3 at their box,
counting from it; ungroup Panel3 right away: both back at their old left/top;
ungroup needs a container), real VS Code 90 (group: the re-drawn tree has the
new panel with both; ungroup Panel2: its buttons in its parent; each undone;
NO-SAVES), probe, panels -- all pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
